     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 5000 mg three times daily comes to 15 g/day, which is almost four times the usual adult maximum of 4 g/day. For a 70 kg adult with normal liver function, a single 5000 mg dose is also well above the usual 1,000 mg maximum. That much acetaminophen risks serious hepatotoxicity and acute liver failure.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **500 mg** PO three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg** PO three times daily (1.95 g/day)\n- **1000 mg** PO three times daily (3 g/day)\n- **1000 mg** PO four times daily (4 g/day, the maximum)\n\nMany clinicians cap at 3 g/day for routine use. If you want a different dose or frequency, tell me and I'll enter it right away. If 5000 mg TID is intentional, for example for a protocol I'm not aware of, please confirm that. I'd also suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
